    "bounding box" : [ 212.2, 453.72, 395.942, 459.751 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "pletely established, the general rule was that a subject was not to"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 12,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 19.0, 450.425, 203.827, 456.65 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "where martial law has not been proclaimed, a person can be"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 66,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 442.212, 396.79, 453.956 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "be tried or punished except by due course of law; all crimes are to be determined by juries subject to the guidance of the judge; that is"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.6, 443.21, 202.849, 449.63 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "sent for trial from such district into a district where martial"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 67,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 436.52, 394.963, 442.551 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "the general rule, and is established law. But from the earliest"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.2, 421.717, 202.871, 442.235 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "law was in operation. It is argued that if the ordinary courts were open and at work in the non-proclaimed district recourse should be had to them. The Privy Council in 1902 (re Marais)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 68,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 419.212, 395.167, 436.362 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "times there was this also which was the law, and is the law still, that when there was a foreign invasion or an insurrection, it was the duty of every good subject, in obedience to the officers and magistrates,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.2, 414.41, 202.462, 420.441 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
