  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 69,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 413.504, 395.216, 418.951 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.444,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "to resist the rebels, . . . in such a case as that of insurrection pre-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.0, 407.21, 202.57, 414.019 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.806,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "had declined to issue a writ of Habeas Corpus in these circum-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 70,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 407.812, 395.853, 413.454 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "vailing so far that the courts of law cannot sit, there must really be"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 71,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 401.812, 396.249, 407.843 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "anarchy unless there is some power to keep the people in order, . . ."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 17.8, 400.01, 203.135, 406.235 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "stances. Mr Justice Blackburn in his Kees in R. v. Eyre"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 72,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 378.906, 395.448, 401.747 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "before that principle the crown claimed the prerogative to exercise summary proceedings by martial law . .. in time of war when this disturbance was going on, over others than the army. And further than that, the crown made this further claim against the insurgents,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.0, 392.811, 202.143, 399.231 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "says,   I have come to the conclusion that, looking at what"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.2, 378.411, 202.536, 391.837 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "martial law was, the bringing of a person into the proclaimed district to be tried might, in a proper case, be justified.  The"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 73,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 373.106, 394.976, 378.942 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "that whilst it existed, pending the insurrection and for a short time"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 17.8, 371.304, 201.337, 377.724 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "learned judge admits that there should bea power of summary"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 74,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.4, 355.799, 395.179, 372.948 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "afterwards, the crown had . . . the power to proclaim martial law in the sense of using summary proceedings, to punish the insurgents and to check and stop the spread of the rebellion by summary pro-"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.0, 364.117, 202.542, 370.342 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "trial, observing all the substantials of justice, in order to stamp"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 18.0, 356.89, 124.124, 362.921 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "out an insurrection by speedy trial."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 24.8, 349.707, 204.452, 356.127 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Whilst martial law is the will of the commanders, and is"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 75,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 349.999, 394.761, 355.835 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "ceedings against the insurgents, soas . . . tostamp out the rebellion."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 76,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 212.0, 344.399, 394.929, 349.652 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.25,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Now no doubt the extent to which the crown had power to do that"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 17.6, 335.303, 202.715, 348.534 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "only limited by the customs of war and the discretion of those who adininister it, still, as far as practicable, the procedure"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 77,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 338.599, 394.983, 344.435 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "has never been yet decided. Our law has been declared from time"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 78,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 332.799, 395.052, 338.441 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.639,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "to time and has always been a practical science, that is, the judges"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 17.6, 306.596, 203.315, 334.328 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "of military law is followed, and a military court is held on the same lines as a court-martial. Charges are simply framed without technicalities. The prisoner is present, the evidence of prosecution and prisoner is taken on oath, the proceedings"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 79,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.4, 321.199, 394.584, 332.927 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 5.833,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "have decided so much as was necessary for the particular case, and that has become part of the law. But it never has come to be decided"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 80,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.6, 315.399, 284.619, 321.43 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "what this precise power is. "
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 81,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 218.2, 307.086, 394.985, 313.506 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.417,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "So far as the United Kingdom is concerned the need has"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 82,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 211.2, 299.997, 393.791, 306.222 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.222,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "never arisen. It has always been found possible to employ"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 17.6, 299.489, 201.776, 305.52 ],
    "font" : "GlyphLessFont",
    "font size" : 6.028,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "are recorded, and the sentence of the court must be confirmed"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
